 "notes": "From the street and garden views (a heavy podium of board-marked concrete with fieldstone set into it, a glazed upper floor under five parallel brick barrel vaults separated by concrete ribs, the vault bands projecting past both long faces as shading eaves, a concrete balcony beam round the upper floor, an open stair up the front, and the water tank standing alone on two concrete legs beside the house) and interiors (double-height hall, floating stair, brick vaults over the upper rooms). Rounds (3 renders): 1 massing; 2 vault ribs added between the five bands so they read as concrete and brick, not a tile roof; 3 against the front photos: denser fieldstone inclusions in the podium, a longer front stair climbing along the podium wall with a solid side, arched glass heads under each vault end. Guessed: all dimensions (from storey and door heights), the site slope (drawn flat), the stair and tank positions relative to the house, the carport as a white box, the pool and trees on the north side, the planting. The south front is taken as the street. The house is placed no closer than its town (Cordoba)."
